4987:
** σωρ-εύω**,
**heap** one thing **on** another, τι πρός τι {{NT+4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1390b18; ἐπὶ τοῦ κοσκίνου τὰ τεθλιμμένα 1st c.AD: Dioscorides (Dioscurides) Medicus 4.150; ἄλλον ἐπ᾽ ἄλλῳ πλοῦτον 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “epigram” 12.6; ἄνθρακας ἐπὶ τὴν κεφαλήν τινος LXX.Pro.25.22, NT.Rom.12.20; περὶ τὸ σῶμα λάφυρα 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Pelopidas” 33; νεκρούς 1st c.BC: Diodorus Siculus Historicus 12.62; πλοῦτον [prev. author] 1.62, compare 5.46, 1st c.BC: Philodemus Philosophus “περὶ οἰκονομίας” p.45 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus}}:—_passive_, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “de Generatione et Corruptione” 325b22, 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 16.11.4; οὐσίας πλῆθος -εύεται 4th-3rd c.BC: Epicurus Philosophus “Fragmenta” 480.}}
**II** **heap with** something, with _genitive_, αἰγιαλοὶ σεσωρευμένοι τινῶν {{NT+2nd c.BC+|2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 16.8.9: with _dative_, σ. βωμοὺς λιβάνῳ 2nd c.AD: Herodianus Grammaticus 4.8.9; αὐχένας στέμμασι “Anthologia Graeca” 7.233 (1st c.AD: Apollonides Epigrammaticus): _metaphorically_, γυναικάρια σεσωρευμένα ἁμαρτίαις NT.2Tim.3.6.}}

4988:
